+        {
+            // G1.8g, and this is the wall. The signal usually arrives with the running thread
+            // still current, but a BLOCK inside the guest clears m_currentThreadId, and the two
+            // cases are opposites:
+            //
+            //   - an override/interrupt queued an invocation and the thread is still Ready or
+            //     Running. Re-establishing the main thread is right: the invocation needs an
+            //     owner, and the guest's own frame is it.
+            //
+            //   - the thread called sce_SleepThread (or waited on a semaphore/event/vsync).
+            //     It is Waiting, and putting it back on the run queue makes the sleep a no-op:
+            //     the main thread never yields, no other thread is ever dispatched, and the
+            //     guest spins in its own idle loop. That is W8, measured as 44579 guest
+            //     entries against 119 syscalls and 469 MMIO accesses.
